cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hep-simlib: checked response libraries and component interaction banks for HEP fast simulation"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
authors:
  - family-names: Mina
    given-names: Rob
    affiliation: "University of Virginia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2241-8566"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobMina/hep-simlib"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  hep-simlib provides checked response libraries for fast simulation (manifests, content hashes, domain accounting, a fidelity vocabulary) and component interaction banks: complete Geant4 trials of a detector component recorded once and replayed exactly in any rigid placement, in Python (float64 and float32) and inside Geant4 through a fast-simulation model. It includes an experiment-neutral Geant4 recorder and validation campaigns on a public toy module.
keywords:
  - "fast simulation"
  - "Geant4"
  - "detector simulation"
  - "response libraries"
  - "particle physics"
  - "JAX"
